{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hey, come on in. I'm Dr. Patel. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Stomach.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's been hurting in his stomach, and he barely sleeps. I'm Marlene, his wife. We nearly turned around, that parking garage is a maze.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (DOCTOR): Glad you stuck it out. Whereabouts does it hurt?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Middle.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right in the middle. And what's it feel like, if you had to describe it?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Burns.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Burns, okay. If you put a number on it, zero to ten, where are you?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Dinner.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ah, so around dinner. I'll let the number go. How long has this burning been going on?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Two weeks.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Two weeks, he says. The burning in the middle, worse at night and after food, it's been more like a month. Started before my sister's party.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay. You two don't quite match, two weeks versus about a month. I'll hold it as somewhere in between, we don't have to fight it out.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): Have you been vomiting at all?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any black stool, or blood when you use the bathroom?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): Fevers? Chills?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He also flops down on the couch the second dinner's done. I tell him not to.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Lying flat after you eat can feed that burn. And the sleep, what's that been like for you?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Bad.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Bad like you can't fall asleep, or you wake up?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Both.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He tosses from about midnight till four. Maybe four hours if he's lucky.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): Has the poor sleep gone on as long as the stomach pain, or longer than that?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Dunno.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): That's fine, we can leave the start date open. Are you on any medicines at the moment?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Well, he was taking ibuprofen, two hundred milligrams, two or three times a day, for five-ish years, for his knee. He stopped it.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): You stopped the ibuprofen. About when?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Recently.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): And urgent care gave him sucralfate, which he never took, not once. His mom takes metformin for her diabetes, that's hers. My sister's biotin for her hair, ignore that.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): We'll leave mom's metformin and your sister's biotin out of his chart, and I won't list sucralfate if he never took it. Any drug allergies?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): How about alcohol?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Socially.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): Socially can mean a glass at a wedding or, you know, more. Which is it for you?",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Honey. Just say it.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): A bottle of wine most nights, perhaps.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): I appreciate you telling me straight. No lecture, I promise. That amount can stir up the stomach and the liver, so I do want liver blood tests. Any surgeries in the past?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any old ulcers, or diabetes yourself?",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'm just going to press on your belly. Soft, tender right in the middle where you said, no guarding.",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (DOCTOR): Blood pressure is one twenty-eight over eighty-two, heart rate seventy-six.",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (DOCTOR): I think this is most likely irritation of the stomach lining, gastritis, possibly an ulcer, given the burning, the wine, and the ibuprofen you were on. I can't say for sure today.",
  "[SEG0050] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'm going to start you on, um, famotidine — actually let's do omeprazole, twenty milligrams by mouth every morning before breakfast, for that burning. And we'll order a liver panel today.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): If you can, ease off the wine, don't lie down right after dinner, and stay off the ibuprofen. I'll see you back in two weeks for the labs. If you vomit blood or the pain turns sharp and severe, go to the ER, don't wait on that visit."
 ],
